---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Panda's Playhouse"
  description="A membership website for an online gaming community that outgrew its Facebook page, built on Wix Studio with Velo so the owners' team could maintain it themselves."
  client="Panda's Playhouse"
  role="UX design & Wix Studio development"
  year="2023"
  slides={[
    {
      title: 'Step 1: Figma design',
      src: '/images/web-development-project-pandas-playhouse-ui-design.png',
      poster: '/images/hifi-img.svg',
      type: 'image',
      alt: "High-fidelity Figma design of the Panda's Playhouse homepage",
    },
    {
      title: 'Step 2: Prototyping',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-pandas-playhouse-prototype.mp4',
      poster: '/images/panda-prototype.svg',
    },
    {
      title: 'Step 3: Development',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-pandas-playhouse-development.mp4',
      poster: '/images/panda-development.svg',
    },
  ]}
  highlights={[
    { value: '5,000+', label: 'Active members moved from Facebook to their own site' },
    { value: 'ID verification', label: 'Third-party facial verification for new sign-ups' },
    { value: 'Members only', label: 'Gated area plus a virtual currency system' },
  ]}
  overview={[
    'Panda\'s Playhouse grew a community of more than 5,000 active members on Facebook ads alone. The next step was a real membership website: <strong>identity verification for new members, a members-only area, a way to convert their virtual currency, and a mobile experience their users would actually enjoy.</strong> The owners also wanted the site built on Wix, so their virtual assistants could update it without hiring developers.',
    'We started with low-fidelity wireframes to settle the flow from landing page to signed-in member, then moved to high-fidelity designs and a clickable prototype in Figma. Only after the flow and color scheme were approved did development start, which kept revisions cheap.',
    'Wix Studio\'s Velo layer let me build the custom pieces on top of the drag-and-drop platform: a facial verification step powered by a third-party API, a gated members area with features hidden from the public, and the currency system members use to cash out. The site is responsive across screen sizes and quick across browsers, and the owners were ecstatic with the result.',
  ]}
  tools={['Wix Studio', 'JavaScript (Velo)', 'Third-party APIs', 'CSS', 'Figma', 'ChatGPT']}
/>
